Identify NCM mode from the owned gadget rather than global IP forwarding.
Upstream: https://codeberg.org/DylanVanAssche/usb-signaller/src/tag/v0.4.2

Other network interfaces may need IP forwarding while the USB gadget stays in
developer mode. Misclassifying it as tethering makes default-mode startup fail
and repeated initialization can delete the newly recreated same-name gadget.
Preserve connected-NBD netboot protection regardless of forwarding policy.

